    },
    "message": "Raise the Python rule's errors from the geometry change check, and compare them\n\ncore/errors.rs (on lane L8a's file) gains value_error, invariant, the one exit\ncorrupt, and relayed for a contract's own error; with errors_switch on, the\nentries that fall back to a Python rule also run it after such an error and\ncount whether the class and text are the same (benchmarks/rule_shadow/\nerror_compare.py). The refusal census also counts what the Python rule raised\nafter each refusal.\n\nvalidate_geometry_change now raises each ValueError of the Python rule in its\norder instead of saying Unsupported; a sweep of changes over the generated plan\ncompares 52 texts with the rule's.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K4QyYRukuCLBerKa4UYj4y",
